	"description": "The Windows navigation layer as it was written by hand in windows/platform/remap/nav_layer.ahk before it became data: one row per hotkey the layer registered, with its #HotIf criterion (layer = LayerEnabled, layer_kana = LayerEnabled and _ALTGR_KANA_FIXUP) and what its body did. send:<text> is the ActionLayer Send string, N standing for AppState_GetNumberOfRepetitions(); repeat_count:<N> is SetNumberOfRepetitions(N); call:maximize_window is WinMaximize(\"A\"). kana_guard marks the RAlt spellings that return while the Kana SC138 key is physically down. Extracted mechanically from the file at commit f4d0bfd63 and frozen: the recommended layer (_shared/keymap/layers.recommended.toml) must still produce exactly these rows.",
